00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:39.910
and eventually crossing over
into over a trillion dollars

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.470
of tax payer money

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:44.670
to fight this unnecessary war.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.370
Saddam Hussein was a really bad guy.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:48.740
He committed mass genocide

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.090
against his own people, the Kurds.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:54.388
He executed many others,
imprisoned many others.

00:15:54.388 --> 00:15:58.500
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.333
- All in all,

00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:01.620
the number of dead on
Saddam Hussein's hands

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.350
numbers around 250,000

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.730
according to Human Rights Watch.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.820
That was over 25 years
of his brutal regime.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.530
And yet in just eight years

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.690
of this war that the US started in Iraq,

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:13.130
way more people were killed.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:17.920
A power vacuum was opened up
that allowed ISIS to thrive,

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:20.130
and for what?

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.920
Why did we do this?

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.500
How was this worth it?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.670
I really believe that in the aftermath

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.930
of those towers falling,

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.170
this group of guys

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.970
began constructing a story for themselves.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:36.000
A fantasy, one not grounded in
real facts from intelligence,

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.260
but one grounded in fear and
in desire to be the hero,

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:44.080
